      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MY GREEK GOD (6) returned a career-high figure two back when a barnstorming second over 2145m at Goulburn. Raced midfield and was a bit one-paced last start over 2200m at Newcastle. Not a lot of depth to this race - he should relish 2400m and prove tough to hold out. MAJORIAN (1) has not raced since finishing third to SABLONNEUSE over 2000m here five weeks ago. Given a tick-over trial since at Randwick. Finds the line well and is a threat stepping up to this distance. SABLONNEUSE (3) scored over 2000m here two back then was there to win but didn't quite finish off over 2200m at Newcastle most recently. Will race handy and give backers a sight. SUNBURNT COUNTRY (4) has been racing well of late, albeit over shorter trips on the Canberra Acton. A few question marks today but going too well to dismiss. ANULFA (5) progressed nicely last start when in the money over 2000m at Wagga at the second run back. Open to further improvement.",
